 "reports_individuals_with_tnfaip3_variant": true,
 "relevance_note": "A 16-patient thalidomide study of monogenic autoinflammatory diseases that includes two HA20 patients described individually in Supplementary file 2 ('TNFAIP3: p. R271X', 'TNFAIP3: p. D70N') and in Table 2 (No 12 and 13).",
 "method_note": "Read by hand; a short script assembled the JSON and copied spans by slicing the paper text. Only the two HA20 patients (No 12 and 13 in Table 2 and Supplementary file 2) are in scope; the other 14 cohort members (other genes) get no rows. Labels 'Case 12'/'Case 13' follow the paper's own text form ('Case 1', 'cases 4,12,13', 'cases 5 and 12'). Supplementary file 2 gives 'Age at baseline in years' (11.50 and 5.75), i.e. age when thalidomide started, followed by 12 months of treatment; this is neither onset, diagnosis nor last evaluation, so those fields are 'not reported'. Table 1 HA20 column gives only counts for the 2 HA20 patients (e.g. Elevated CRP 1, Elevated ESR 1, Immunosuppressive agents 1, Others 1 = hydroxychloroquine, Glucocorticoids 0); these were not assigned to either person, and zero counts exclude no one. Table 2 disease severity of HA20: No 12 'Mild' at baseline then 'Disease-free activity'; No 13 'Moderate' at baseline, 'Moderate' at 9 months, 'Disease-free activity' at 12 months; not recorded as features. 'Fever' as listed per patient was not mapped to the checklist item 'recurrent fever' (recurrence not stated per person); 'hypothyroidism' was not mapped to 'autoimmune thyroiditis'; 'multiple nodules in both lungs' was not mapped to interstitial lung disease; 'punctate erosion of the rectum' was mapped to 'gastrointestinal ulcers or inflammation'. Peripheral neuropathy and somnolence are excluded from the safety statement 'None of the patients had adverse events such as peripheral neuropathy and somnolence' (whole named group, during thalidomide treatment). Anorexia and nausea for Case 12 are thalidomide adverse events, not disease features. Variant fields: protein-only strings with a space after 'p.' are kept as printed; no transcript, zygosity, inheritance or classification is given. cites_prior_report_of_same_patients is null: the paper does not say these patients were described before (ref [17] describes two other HA20 patients treated with thalidomide, without individual detail; not in scope). No stacked cells. No internal contradictions found.",
